  "final_answer_preview": "The distinction between kidnapping and abduction is defined in the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023. Kidnapping is described in Section 137(2) as taking a person from India or from lawful guardianship, punishable by imprisonment for up to seven years and a fine. In contrast, abduction is defined in Section 138 as compelling or inducing a person to leave a place by force or deceitful means. This indicates that kidnapping is more about the unlawful removal of a person, while abduction focuses on the coercive or deceptive act of leading someone away.",
